# .envrc template for a dev shell that lives in this dendritic flake.
#
# Copy to your project root as .envrc, then replace the two placeholders:
#   __FLAKE_REF__   flake URI + shell attr, e.g. ~/NixConfig#drpom
#   __SHELL_NAME__  the devShells attr name (see table below)
#
# Requires nix-direnv on PATH:
#   nix profile install nix-direnv
# or enable programs.direnv.nixDirEnv in your Nix config.
#
# Shells available (declared in dendritic/dev-shells/*.nix):
#   android  x86_64-linux                  android-tools, payload-dumper-go
#   drpom    x86_64-linux, aarch64-darwin node/pnpm/eas/deno/kotlin/railway/psql
#   yt-dlp   x86_64-linux, aarch64-darwin mutagen, drives the yt-dlp sync
#
# aarch64-linux (nix-on-droid) has none of these. Asking for a shell your system
# does not define fails with:
#   error: flake '...' does not provide attribute 'devShells.<system>.<shell>.name'
# There is no devShells.default anywhere, so `#<attr>` is mandatory; omit it and
# nix looks for 'devShells.<system>.default' and fails the same way.
#
# `-v --log-format internal-json` pipes nix's log into nom. Drop both flags for a
# plain shell.
#
# CACHE WARNING: nix-direnv 3.1.2 watches only flake.nix, flake.lock and
# devshell.toml. Editing dendritic/dev-shells/<shell>.nix does NOT invalidate the
# direnv cache, so you get a stale shell with no warning. Run `direnv reload`
# by hand after changing any module under dendritic/.

use flake __FLAKE_REF__ -v --log-format internal-json 2> >(nom --json)

# Project-specific exports go below. The shell's own shellHook has already run by
# the time this line is reached, and `unset LD` below drops the nix-provided LD so
# macOS system binaries resolve normally.
#
# export PROJECT_VAR=...
# unset LD